"""kmixdeck-web — the browser frontend's bridge (ADR 0011, AR-8/AR-9).

Speaks ONLY D-Bus to the daemon (AR-6: no PipeWire here) and serves the web UI plus one WebSocket per browser tab.

Wire protocol (JSON text frames, one object per frame):
  client → server   {"op":"hello","token":"…"}                      first frame; token required when bound to the LAN
                    {"op":"set","path":"/org/kmixdeck1/channels/mic","property":"Trim","value":0.7}
                    {"op":"call","path":"/org/kmixdeck1","method":"AddChannel","args":["Music"],"id":7}
  server → client   {"op":"snapshot","state":{…}}                    the whole view model once, right after hello
                    {"op":"patch","state":{…}}                       RFC 7386 merge patch — apply over the last state
                    {"op":"meters","peaks":{"channel/mic":0.31,…}}   the daemon's 25 Hz Peaks signal, forwarded
                    {"op":"loudness","loudness":{"stream":[-23.1,-22.8,-21.4,-6.2]}}   UX-18: EBU R128 per mix
                    {"op":"result","id":7,"ok":true,"value":…}       reply to a call
                    {"op":"error","id":7,"message":"…"}

The view model is the D-Bus object tree, verbatim: `state.objects[path][Property] = value`, plus `state.root` for
the Mixer root object — the same names the KDE window, the tray popover and the Stream Deck plugin read (AR-9).
A feature added to the daemon shows up here with no bridge work at all.

Only org.kmixdeck1.* interfaces are reachable, and only their writable properties and declared methods: there is no
"call anything on the bus" endpoint (ADR 0011 §2). The allowlist is read from the daemon's own introspection.
Methods that take a file descriptor (`h`, Channel.Play) are not in it: an fd cannot travel over a WebSocket.

CT-10, opt-in `--play HOST:PORT`: a SECOND listener, plain HTTP, with its own token (`play-token`, never the web-UI
token), that can do exactly one thing — play an uploaded audio file into a channel whose Playback switch is on
(ADR 0016). It cannot move a fader, read state beyond that, or reach any other method:
  POST /channel/<slug>/play[?title=…]   Authorization: Bearer <play token>, Content-Length required, body = the file
       → blocks until the track ended: 200 played · 410 stopped · 422 error: … (JSON {"ok","id","result"})
  GET  /healthz                         no auth: 200 {"ok":true} while the daemon is on the bus, else 503
"""
